# TWO REACT MAJORS IN ONE STORE, AND THEY MUST NOT SHARE A TYPES COPY.
#
# apps/web is a Next 15 app on React 19; apps/mobile is Expo 52 / RN 0.76 and
# is pinned to React 18 by its toolchain. Both are correct.
#
# pnpm gives the virtual store ONE hoisted `@types/react` for packages that
# declare React types as an optional peer. Whichever major won that symlink
# poisoned the other app's compile: a program holding two copies of
# @types/react produces the structurally identical but nominally different
# ReactNode that makes every forwardRef component "not a valid JSX element
# type" (TS2786). That was the whole of the 179-error web typecheck, and it is
# a resolution fault, not a code fault.
#
# The fallback is therefore removed, and each app's tsconfig pins `react` /
# `react-dom` to its OWN copy (see the `paths` entries and the note beside
# them). Every file in a program then resolves one copy, whichever app it is.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
